Expected elements: present

Four panes, the Call Trace/Event Log tab strip with Call Trace open, Values outside that strip, both stepping directions, scrubber, phase rail, the chain exit, and the `Data` row with its `Synthetic demo data` badge are all present. Body text is strong (7.3–19:1). The faults are decoration and role reuse.

(a) Confirmed, narrowly. In the TRANSACTION pane the fade lands on a line fully inside the box — "only proofs, nullifiers and commitments are", y874–885, nine pixels clear of the border at y895 — ramping 4.54:1 to 2.05:1 (x-height mean 3.11:1); a further line at y892 sits at 1.10:1. That is the honesty prose, graded as content. Refuted: every pane bottom border measures #A2A2A2 at full strength, identical to its top border; the mask does not erase the boundary. Code fades only the genuinely clipped line 52; Values does not fade. No RAW block at 900px, so that claim is untestable here.

Glyphs, re-measured independently: ⊙/⊘ IoU 0.781, ink mass 26.5 vs 30.7 alpha-px (14.7%), 7 differing pixels inside a 4×4 interior, identical at 1×, separated only by colour (#484848 vs #0E7490). ⊙ ring flanks 1.60–2.71:1, caps 4.29:1. The coverage dot `·` is #1A7B95 — same hue, three levels apart — and is ⊙'s own centre. Cyan carries six meanings across five values.

Fixes: exempt the last full line from the mask; redesign the position glyph.

Rating: 4/10

